cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below.
type: software
title: "launch-cumulative-screening: a stochastic-scheduling framework for cumulative-effects screening of high-cadence launch and landing operations"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-12-07"
authors:
  - family-names: Gupta
    given-names: Avin
    affiliation: Independent researcher
    email: iamavingupta@gmail.com
license:
  - BSD-3-Clause
  - CC-BY-4.0
license-url: https://github.com/AvinGupta-ship-it/launch-cumulative-screening/blob/main/LICENSE
repository-code: https://github.com/AvinGupta-ship-it/launch-cumulative-screening
abstract: >-
  Code in this repository (src/, scripts/, figures/, tests/, configs/) is licensed
  under the BSD 3-Clause License. Text, figures and derived data (paper/, comment/,
  docs/, data/transcribed/, data/processed/, results/) are licensed under the
  Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License. The framework treats
  launch and landing operations as a marked point process on the calendar,
  evaluates additive, energy-averaged, number-above, exceedance-day, coverage and
  interval metrics plus public-access availability, and quantifies the error of
  extrapolating per-operation or annual-average assessments linearly to higher
  cadence, with a global sensitivity analysis over the uncertain inputs. Applied
  to the proposed increase in Starship-Super Heavy operations at the Boca Chica
  Launch Site (FAA docket FAA-2026-12808).
keywords:
  - cumulative effects
  - NEPA
  - launch noise
  - point processes
  - sensitivity analysis
